      "writtenOn": "2026-06-10T14:57:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point, and I agree, I think we do not need a partition-specific replay method.\n\nFor example, in Kafka, `replayAllEvents(topic)` does not compute partitions itself. \n\nIt finds the active subscribers for that topic and calls `resetOffset()` on each one. Then each subscriber rewinds to the beginning of its current Kafka `assignment()`.\n\nThis is already existing code [here](https://github.com/GerritForge/events-kafka/blob/master/src/main/java/com/gerritforge/gerrit/plugins/kafka/subscribe/KafkaEventNativeSubscriber.java#L193).",
